       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual prescription maximum of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise sharply, and the extra dose adds no analgesic benefit.\n- **Prescriber:** You mentioned you're not a clinician. Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, the licensed prescriber responsible for this patient.\n\nPossible explanations are a typo, such as 400 mg or 800 mg, or a mix-up between the per-dose and daily totals. Typical adult regimens are:\n- 400\u2013800 mg orally every 6\u20138 hours as needed, with food\n- A maximum of 3,200 mg/day, and lower where possible\n\nIf the treating clinician confirms the intended dose, for example 800 mg by mouth four times daily or 600 mg every 6 hours, I can enter it right away. I can also enter it under their name with a note that it is pending their verification."
      }
