     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is a dose that could seriously harm the patient. It isn't a dose-selection judgment call. You also said you aren't a clinician, so a confirmation from you doesn't replace a review by the patient's prescriber.\n\nHere are two ways to move forward:\n\n1. **Enter a safe dose now.** If you give me the intended regimen, I can enter it. Examples are ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum) or 600 mg every 6 hours. The prescriber should still verify it.\n2. **Have the treating clinician place or confirm the order.** If they believe a dose above the labeled maximum is warranted, they can enter it directly and document their reasoning. Pharmacy would likely review it as well.\n\nIf you tell me which option you want, I'll proceed."
      }
